 they did with michael's storyline  and character  is that he's trying to have his cake and  eat it too  meaning this episode really develops  well that he wants his son to go free  not get caught for what he did but he  doesn't want anyone else taking the  blame for  it and that's kofi so there is a ounce  of humanity left in michael  and that he's still trying to do the  right thing for kofi  while clearing his son's name so it  complicates things even more  i think it would have been really boring  if they just went with him full-on  committing to letting other people take  the blame but  it makes it so much more interesting  that he's trying to  somehow do the right thing in all the  things he's messing up on and that's why  it made it so interesting having  this lee story develop now with kofi  which we'll get into  but it's interesting that charlie here  flips out  on michael saying now you're gonna get  me in trouble  i was helping out i'm involved with this  felony here  what is your problem for getting lee  involved but it's almost like michael  takes from charlie  this little moment he says that are you  banging lee  and that's the only way you're going to  manage her because he ends up kissing  liability in this episode he definitely  was already into her but  i feel like he's going to escalate  things because he knows he's going to  have to keep an eye on her and make sure  she's just following the path he set out  for her  i also think it's hysterical when we go  back to adam's story that  he is still developing photos in a dark  room in 2020  and i get what they were doing  artistically with him having  a vision of him dancing and being free  but  i'm going to act like that didn't happen  because it just came off comical to me i  was laughing at  seeing hunter doing show off his dance  moves here i also think it's  really strange that the character of  franny who's his teacher that we know  from episode one he's been sleeping with  that they cast her as someone who looks  exactly the same age  as adam it's a little puzzling and  confusing because there's a subconscious  part of me and i think other viewers can  relate where you think  she's like a co-student and it makes it  look less scandalous as it being a  teacher  which it should look and it's also  strange because there's a line here  where michael says to franny  you know when his mom died you were  there for him you comforted him i think  that would have worked as an older  figure it's kind of just  not giving the effect i feel like it  needs by having someone who looks  exactly the same age  but we'll see how it plays out now two  scenes that really stood out to me the  first one  is i love all these 10 scenes that we  have is detective costello here  played by amy landecker and she has  another good one here at the dinner  table  with adam and michael i think all fans  of breaking bad and brian cranston are  going to love scenes where  michael has his back against the woman  has to talk his way out of it just like  walter white always had to do  and you see detective castell is clearly  suspicious of michael and adam and  that's what i'm loving about what this  show's doing right now is it's  adding so many factions here that can  mess everything up for michael there's  so many  layers and moving parts and it makes it  that more interesting in a story that i  was worried could get bland because we  already know what happened at the crime  scene but  they're making it really intriguing and  how many  parties are involved and how many things  can mess up our protagonists here  in michael and his plan now my favorite  scene of brian cranston so far acting  wise  end of hunter doing here is when adam  calls out michael  for acting and pretending like  everything's normal and okay  and brings up that tomorrow is a funeral  for the boy he killed and i love he's  like so we're just gonna pretend they're  not burying him tomorrow and michael  goes  yes yes that