r played by hope davis who  does a great job this episode  really takes the spotlight now and we  get now  brought into the story of carlo baxter  the brother who's in jail  now gina has this brilliant plan this is  what she says in the episode is gonna be  their big move to just  end this conflict they think with this  gang is that  she's gonna get her son to the funeral  so she got a moment to whisper to him  and tell him to take care of kofi and we  see gina's this mastermind cause she's  bribing people here to even get him at  this funeral  and she's got her head more on her  shoulders and a plan of action where  jimmy baxter is broken right now and we  even see him say a line here that he  feels guilt for his son's death because  he bought him that bike but  you see gina here just instead of being  a  sad mom they've given her character now  a motive and an eye on the ball here  where  jimmy's kind of the one flustered so  where the story lines now that we've  talked about so far all come together  is really effective in one episode at  this  funeral scene and everything ramps up  now because now michael's putting it  together  his fear of already hearing carlo baxter  might go this funeral earlier in the  episode  now he sees he's there so he literally  runs  to make a phone call to get kofi moved  because he knows exactly  what the baxters are planning here but  remember this gets messed up his  protection plan of moving kofi because  he's talking to an unreliable  cop on the other end who's more focused  on the sports game so we can assume that  he didn't get kofi  moved in time but that's why it's so  important that kofi's prison mate here  who's looking out for him  basically gives him really good advice  that you're not gonna beat the baxters  you know  they're dangerous in every facet but we  can assume he's told kofi to  try to make some kind of deal and just  go talk to him  carlo bax before he just whacks you so  that leads to the end of this episode 